                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e7fd215e-6aea-3019-b19d-3d4c7daf0986",
                        "entry_id": "b2088d65-0504-328c-84fa-3cd2cf454044",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To perform on stage; to act in a play."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "41b39bbe-d2d4-391c-9fd6-de3efcc08fa9",
                        "entry_id": "b2088d65-0504-328c-84fa-3cd2cf454044",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To play (a scene, role etc.); to act out."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ddd622fb-b99e-4e66-8047-c7d08e1a9c5a",
                                "sense_id": "41b39bbe-d2d4-391c-9fd6-de3efcc08fa9",
                                "text": "Kelly’s involvement made it a song not only about fame, but also about alleged sex across creepy power differentials. This wasn’t really even subtext: Gaga and Kelly playacted an Oval Office affair at the American Music Awards."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "45725581-47af-3671-9a3a-1b76dca60110",
                        "entry_id": "b2088d65-0504-328c-84fa-3cd2cf454044",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To engage in pretence or insincere behavior, often in order to mislead someone or gain an advantage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f041119f-75b1-45e0-8479-df9d33efef83",
                                "sense_id": "45725581-47af-3671-9a3a-1b76dca60110",
                                "text": "The most Trump can imagine selling is himself, and what that self is is merely a hologram, a weightless shape. He play-acts at being a businessman. He play-acts at being a president. The only thing that’s authentic about him is his comic-book worldview, one divided between heroes and villains, us and them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "87cee8bd-626b-4db6-bb43-b90803933a6e",
                                "sense_id": "45725581-47af-3671-9a3a-1b76dca60110",
                                "text": "Abby, watching Harper give the closeted performance that she’s been giving her whole life, sees a side of her that she doesn’t like — the one who play-acts and denies herself almost too well."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d22a9693-7770-4fac-b2db-0b2a21e1b005",
                                "sense_id": "45725581-47af-3671-9a3a-1b76dca60110",
                                "text": "Little girls aren’t taught to play-act at being queen. They play-act at being princesses, which is a much gauzier, more romantic kind of role."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3cadde3b-13d6-3b7d-9d26-20a4adc8f6a9",
                        "entry_id": "b2088d65-0504-328c-84fa-3cd2cf454044",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make a pretence of; to feign or simulate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b6acaed-26a7-4b9e-b9a6-231e27d71525",
                                "sense_id": "3cadde3b-13d6-3b7d-9d26-20a4adc8f6a9",
                                "text": "If the devil’s advocate playacts disagreement with you for the sake of strengthening your argument, the concern troll is his mirror image, a person who pretends to agree with you in order to undermine you."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85053dff-3625-43cd-9618-622a8aee93e6",
                                "sense_id": "3cadde3b-13d6-3b7d-9d26-20a4adc8f6a9",
                                "text": "Asked after the match if Djokovic had been play-acting the symptoms of cramp, Murray replied “I don't know. I would hope that that wouldn't be the case. But, yeah, if it was cramp, that's a tough thing to recover from and play as well as he did at the end.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
